    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0607" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v07/pg573"/>

                <head>273. Telegram From Secretary of State to the Embassy in Bolivia<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d273-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-09-28T19:29:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                                1956—7:29 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>96. Department agrees objectives of action recommended Embtel 93<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d273-f2"/> but doubts whether prospects of success justify risks
                    involved, including misinterpretation as intervention in internal Bolivian
                    affairs. You may state following if approached by Bolivian leaders or if
                    opportunity otherwise presented discuss problem with them.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Department concerned over indications possible imminent change in
                        Government but recognizes this internal Bolivian matter.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Any changes would naturally require thorough evaluation in terms US
                        policies.</item>
                </list>
                <p>FYI basic elements such evaluation would be (1) that communists or communist
                    sympathizers do not participate in or have influence in government; and (2) that
                    stabilization program be carried out.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
